Lab 11: Managing Dynamic Inventories
Objectives

By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

    Understand the concept and benefits of dynamic inventories in Ansible compared to static inventories
    Configure and test a dynamic inventory source using the Ansible aws_ec2 inventory plugin
    Create and execute Ansible playbooks that consume dynamic inventory data
    Troubleshoot common dynamic inventory configuration issues using a diagnostic script
    Apply dynamic inventory concepts to a new, independent scenario

Prerequisites

Before starting this lab, students should have:

    Basic understanding of Ansible fundamentals (playbooks, inventory, modules)
    Familiarity with AWS services (EC2, IAM) - a sandbox or lab AWS account is sufficient
    Knowledge of YAML syntax and JSON data structures
    Experience with Linux command line operations
    Completion of previous Ansible labs or equivalent experience

Required software (install if not already present in your lab environment):

python3 -m pip install --user boto3 botocore
ansible-galaxy collection install amazon.aws

Verify the collection installed correctly:

ansible-doc -t inventory -l | grep aws_ec2

Expected output: a line similar to amazon.aws.aws_ec2 followed by a short description.

This lab is performed entirely in an isolated, self-owned practice environment (an Al Nafi cloud machine or your own sandbox AWS account) for defensive, educational purposes: understanding how dynamic inventories work helps you correctly configure, audit, and secure automation pipelines that manage cloud infrastructure.
